<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23084" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-exspectātus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inexp-</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>unexpected</i> (class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Of persons: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in armis Hostis adest,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					12, 65</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of
			inanim. and abstr. things: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quanta vis! quam inexspectata!</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Or. 2, 55, 225</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nihil insolitum, nihil inexspectatum est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Ep. 107</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 2, 22</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. 8, 3, 74</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">accidisse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					9, 2, 24</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
